# Portability

Application, `products/`, `platform/protocols/`, and `platform/services/` must not include:

- `<pthread.h>`, `<semaphore.h>` (except inside `osal/posix/`)
- FreeRTOS headers (except inside `osal/freertos/`)
- ESP-IDF headers (`esp_*`, `driver/twai.h`, NimBLE) except inside `platform/drivers/esp32/` and `ports/esp32_c3/`

Use OSAL (`os_thread`, `os_mutex`, `os_queue`, …) and HAL (`hal_can`, `hal_uart`, …) only.

```c
/* BAD — in uds.c or a product */
#include <pthread.h>
#include "freertos/FreeRTOS.h"
#include "driver/twai.h"

/* GOOD */
#include "os_thread.h"
#include "hal_can.h"
```

CAN IDs in `ae_can_ids.h` are prototype/simulated, never claimed as OEM.
Do not claim ISO 26262 or WP.29 certification.
